#: processes/crdm-needs.bpmn:20
#. Diagram element documentation
msgid "Drafts the needs statement but never decides it is right — A_Synthesise is the sole target when GW_Needs loops back — and this process's own documentation calls an unconfirmed synthesis \"an agent's summary, not a requirement,\" which is exactly what this lane alone produces before the two lanes below it look at it."
msgstr ""

#: processes/crdm-needs.bpmn:41
#. Diagram element documentation
msgid "From the chat, issue, uploads and library sources, write a clear, jargon-free statement of what is needed and why, tied to a concrete workflow. Post it on the GitHub issue, not in chat, and ask the requester and stakeholders to review it."
msgstr ""

#: processes/crdm-needs.bpmn:13
#. Diagram element documentation
msgid "Identify the stakeholders, synthesise a needs statement from the sources, and loop until the BA and the stakeholders both recognise it. The loop is the phase: a needs statement nobody confirmed is an agent's summary, not a requirement."
msgstr ""

#: processes/crdm-needs.bpmn:33
#. Diagram label
msgid "Phase 1: Identify stakeholders"
msgstr ""

#: processes/crdm-needs.bpmn:39
#. Diagram label
msgid "Phase 1: Synthesise needs from sources"
msgstr ""

#: processes/crdm-needs.bpmn:32
#. Diagram label
msgid "Phase begins"
msgstr ""

#: processes/crdm-needs.bpmn:55
#. Diagram label
msgid "Phase complete"
msgstr ""

#: processes/crdm-needs.bpmn:44
#. Diagram label
msgid "Review synthesised needs statement"
msgstr ""

#: processes/crdm-needs.bpmn:61
#. Diagram label
msgid "revise"
msgstr ""

#: processes/crdm-needs.bpmn:27
#. Diagram label
msgid "Stakeholders"
msgstr ""

#: processes/crdm-needs.bpmn:52
#. Diagram element documentation
msgid "Stakeholders confirm, on the issue, that the needs statement says what they need — or say what to change. A stakeholder's judgement; an agent does not record it for them."
msgstr ""

#: processes/crdm-needs.bpmn:35
#. Diagram element documentation
msgid "The agent asks the BA who is affected by this change. The BA knows the domain — the agent does not guess."
msgstr ""

#: processes/crdm-needs.bpmn:46
#. Diagram element documentation
msgid "The BA reviews what the agent synthesised and checks it against what they actually need."
msgstr ""

#: processes/crdm-needs.bpmn:16
#. Diagram element documentation
msgid "The single review here is what GW_Needs is literally named for — \"BA approves?\" — even though Lane_Stakeholders' confirmation sits between this task and that gateway in the flow; the phase's own documentation makes clear the loop needs both, so reading the gate label alone would miss half of what it takes to exit it."
msgstr ""

#: processes/crdm-needs.bpmn:28
#. Diagram element documentation
msgid "The task itself carries no documentation of its own, so this lane's entry is the only place recording what \"confirm\" means in Phase 1: recognising the synthesised needs statement as actually theirs, immediately before the loop gate — not, as in the later data-model phase, judging a cardinality, because there is no model yet to have one."
msgstr ""

#: processes/crdm-needs.bpmn:62
#. Diagram label
msgid "yes"
